4435.stem:
Frankie borrows \$200 000 from a bank. The loan is to be repaid over 23 years at a rate of $7.2\%$ per annum, compounded monthly. The repayments have been set at \$1485 per month.

The interest charged and the balance owing for the first three months of the loan are shown in the spreadsheet below.

\extable{271_q36_t1}

parts.latex:
Select the sheet named ‘Regular Extra Payments’ from the options at the bottom of the spreadsheet to answer part d).

If Kim makes an extra repayment of $\$50$ per month in addition to the monthly payment, does the term of the loan increase or decrease and by how much?

\begin{itemize}
\item Input 50 in cell B7 to enter the extra payment amount.
\end{itemize}

Select the sheet named ‘Fortnightly Payments’ from the bottom menu in the spreadsheet to answer parts e) and f)

\begin{itemize}
\item Set up the spreadsheet to find the total repayments and interest

\begin{itemize}
\item In cell F1, enter the formula =sum(C12:C653) to calculate the total amount of repayments.
\item In cell F2, enter the formula =sum(D12:D653) to calculate the total amount of interest paid.
\end{itemize}
\end{itemize}

Kim’s friend Suzy suggests that she can save on her home loan by simply changing the frequency of her repayments to fortnightly instead of monthly.

Is Suzy’s claim true? Justify you answer with reference to the interest paid.
